  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p><b>Assign suitable EC2 instance tags to each server in the Auto Scaling group</b>, <b>Prepare an Auto Scaling group configured with an appropriate instance range and custom AMI if needed</b>, and <b>Ensure there is a valid IAM service role in place</b> are the correct three tasks that must be completed before creating the CodeDeploy Deployment Group:</p><ul><li><b>Assign suitable EC2 instance tags…</b> CodeDeploy identifies which EC2 instances to deploy to by matching tags, so tagging is essential before deployment setup.</li><li><b>Prepare an Auto Scaling group…</b> The group with minimum and maximum instance settings ensures there are enough servers available and incorporates any custom AMI with necessary software pre-installed.</li><li><b>Ensure there is a valid IAM service role…</b> CodeDeploy requires a dedicated IAM role to interact with AWS resources; the role must have the CodeDeploy trust and permissions policies.</li></ul><p>Why the other choices are incorrect:</p><ul><li><i>Create and configure an SNS topic for notification purposes…</i> While SNS notifications are a useful feature during deployments, it is <b>not a mandatory prerequisite</b> for creating the Deployment Group in CodeDeploy.</li><li><i>Set up the Elastic Load Balancer in advance…</i> While configuring a load balancer is <b>recommended</b> for high availability, it is <b>not a strict requirement prior to creating the Deployment Group</b>. It can be added later or is only required if you want to reroute traffic during deployment; in-place deployments can proceed without attaching a load balancer.</li></ul><p><strong>Tip:</strong> Always double-check IAM role permissions and tagging before launching deployment groups to ensure targeting and access work as expected.</p>",
  "query": "<p>A small company wants to use AWS CodeDeploy for a project analyzing customer preferences in car selection. The application environment will use a load balancer (either CLB, ALB, or NLB) and an Auto Scaling group to maintain a minimum of four and up to eight EC2 instances for high availability. The company’s AWS engineer plans to use an in-place deployment. Which THREE steps must the AWS engineer complete before setting up the CodeDeploy Deployment Group from the AWS console?</p>",
  "original_oid": "6793da7a61969b416038a215",
